Subject: mysys: include <cstdlib> for the std:: functions it calls
Last-Update: 2026-09-27

my_malloc.cc calls std::malloc, std::calloc, std::realloc and std::free and
includes only <stdlib.h>, which declares them in the global namespace.
<cstdlib> declares them in std. Earlier libc++ releases brought <cstdlib>
in through other standard headers; libc++ 23 does not, and the file does not
compile against it. It includes the header it uses.

diff --git a/mysys/my_malloc.cc b/mysys/my_malloc.cc
index c2f72e3..aea00ed 100644
--- a/mysys/my_malloc.cc
+++ b/mysys/my_malloc.cc
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@
   @file mysys/my_malloc.cc
 */
 
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <errno.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <string.h>
